{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\nclass ListValidator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def validate_numeric_list(data: list) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(data, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n        if not data:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n        for item in data:\n            if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n                raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\nclass MedianCalculator:\n    def calculate(self, data: list) -> Union[float, int]:\n        ListValidator.validate_numeric_list(data)\n        \n        sorted_data = sorted(data)\n        n = len(sorted_data)\n        \n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            return sorted_data[n // 2]\n        else:\n            mid1 = sorted_data[n // 2 - 1]\n            mid2 = sorted_data[n // 2]\n            return (mid1 + mid2) / 2\n\ndef median(l: list) -> Union[float, int]:\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = MedianCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate(l)"}
